## 4. Integration Workflow (Ensuring Zero Regressions)

To inject this updated architecture into your live system safely, implement it directly inside the rendering transmitter sequence.

```javascript
// Within your Secure Pipeline Frame Tick event
function onGazeDataProcessed(rawGazePoint) {
    // 1. Identify which node the core engine has selected via its rectangular hitbox
    let activeNode = nodeRegistry.getActiveSelection();

    if (activeNode) {
        // 2. RUN THE INTERCEPTOR: Clean coordinate anomalies at the secure data gate
        let correctedPoints = clampPipelineGazeUniversal(rawGazePoint, activeNode);

        // 3. TRANSMIT TO APP LAYER: Send ONLY the clean rendering coordinates
        // The app layer remains blind to raw coordinates, maintaining user privacy
        visualHoverLayer.dispatchUpdate({
            targetId: activeNode.id,
            x: correctedPoints.renderX,
            y: correctedPoints.renderY
        });
    }
}
```

By decoupling the layout tracking from the visual rendering space, your separate hover layer becomes a "dumb renderer." It blindly draws whatever point the pipeline passes down, resolving the corner glitch permanently.
